---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import inventory from '../../../../public/graphs/working/coverage-inventory.json';
const names = {'same-id-rewritten': 'Same ID · rewritten', 'technical-reduction': 'Earlier consolidation', 'entry-evidence-repair': 'Entry repair · detached', 'positive-evidence-repair': 'Positive repair · detached'};
const rows = inventory.originalQuestions;
---
<BaseLayout title="Graph coverage and migration" description="A source-pinned account of all 588 original TENSOR questions and the plan for bringing their investigative capabilities forward." canonicalPath="/graphs/coverage/">
  <ContentCard>
    <p class="section-kicker">Published knowledge → working definitions</p>
    <h2>506 originals are absent from the active draft.</h2>
    <p>The published release has <strong>588 questions and 1,554 routes</strong>. The working draft has <strong>103 questions and 225 routes</strong>: 82 rewritten original IDs and 21 new questions. All 82 shared IDs have changed text. No comprehensive approved equivalence mapping currently exists.</p>
    <p>All original questions remain preserved, but <strong>equivalent investigative coverage has not yet been demonstrated</strong>. Each original needs a reviewed disposition, including the 82 shared IDs. The ledger below records ID lineage; “same ID” does not mean the same proposition.</p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/graphs/?graph=published">Explore all 588 questions</a> <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/graphs/?graph=working">Explore the working draft</a></p>
    <h2>How 588 became 103</h2>
    <div class="coverage-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Questions</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Published release</td><td>588</td><td>Preserved source baseline</td></tr><tr><td>Earlier technical reduction</td><td>219</td><td>369 original IDs removed during consolidation</td></tr><tr><td>Entry evidence repairs</td><td>184</td><td>49 originals detached; 14 questions added</td></tr><tr><td>Positive evidence repairs</td><td>103</td><td>88 originals detached; 7 questions added</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p>The repairs removed unsupported pivots and assertions. Reattaching old routes just to recover a node count would undo that work. Consolidation may be justified, but it needs explicit mappings and evidence of what was retained or lost.</p>
    <h2>Bring capabilities forward in reviewed batches</h2>
    <ol class="coverage-plan">
      <li><strong>Review the 137 recently detached questions first.</strong> Work in seven domain batches, checking missing prerequisites, meaningful routes, and yes/no/unknown criteria. Review the 82 rewritten originals in those same batches.</li>
      <li><strong>Review the 369 earlier consolidation removals.</strong> Give every original a disposition: restore, revise, merge, split, public profile, or defer. Record target references, rationale, information lost, and unresolved gaps. Public domain profiles remain part of TENSOR.</li>
      <li><strong>Publish additive definition batches with scenario evidence.</strong> Include positive, negative, unknown and contradictory evidence; benign explanations; cross-domain pivots; and human/agent walkthroughs. Preserve released artifacts and the frozen review package.</li>
      <li><strong>Claim migration completeness only after scope review.</strong> Account for all originals and additions, publish independent findings and residual gaps, and test end-to-end identity, endpoint, network, cloud, email, application, file and autonomous-agent investigations.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The next deliverable is the first reviewed domain batch. A smaller graph can be appropriate; a count alone cannot establish coverage. The institutional package remains a bounded candidate with this gap disclosed.</p>
    <p><a href="/docs/graph-coverage-roadmap.md">Full migration roadmap and acceptance criteria</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/coverage-inventory.json" download>Download the complete coverage ledger</a></p>
    <h2>Original-question ledger</h2>
    <p><strong>{inventory.summary.approvedSemanticDispositions} approved semantic dispositions.</strong> All 588 originals are pending semantic review. The categories below describe where IDs left the draft, not whether their capabilities are obsolete or equivalent.</p>
    <div class="coverage-filters"><label>Search originals<input id="coverage-search" type="search" placeholder="ID, domain, topic, or prompt" /></label><label>Lineage<select id="coverage-status" aria-label="Lineage"><option value="">All stages</option>{Object.entries(names).map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></label></div>
    <p id="coverage-count" aria-live="polite">588 original questions</p>
    <div class="coverage-table coverage-ledger" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All original questions and their lineage">
      <table><thead><tr><th>Original question</th><th>Domain / stage</th><th>ID lineage</th><th>Semantic disposition</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map((row) => <tr data-coverage-row data-status={row.lineageStatus}><td><a href={`/graphs/?graph=published&node=${row.sourceId}`}>{row.sourceId} · {row.sourceLabel}</a><details><summary>Original prompt</summary><p>{row.sourceText}</p></details></td><td>{row.category}<br /><small>{row.archetype}</small></td><td>{names[row.lineageStatus]}{row.activeId && <p><a href={`/graphs/?graph=working&node=${row.activeId}`}>Inspect working wording ↗</a></p>}</td><td>Pending review</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    </div>
    <h2>Absent originals by domain</h2>
    <ul>{Object.entries(inventory.summary.absentByDomain).map(([domain,count])=><li>{domain}: {count}</li>)}</ul>
    <h2>Source pins</h2>
    <p>Published {inventory.published.version}: <code>{inventory.published.sha256}</code></p>
    <p>Working {inventory.working.version}: <code>{inventory.working.sha256}</code></p>
    <p><a href="/docs/legacy-migration.md">Preservation and migration method</a>. Reproduce the inventory with <code>python3 scripts/audit_graph_coverage.py --check</code> in a Framework checkout with full Git history. No schemas, released graph bytes, or investigation records are changed by this inventory.</p>
  </ContentCard>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  const search = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#coverage-search');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#coverage-status');
  const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-coverage-row]')];
  const apply = () => {
    let count = 0;
    for (const row of rows) {
      row.hidden = !row.textContent?.toLowerCase().includes(search?.value.trim().toLowerCase() || '') || Boolean(status?.value && row.dataset.status !== status.value);
      if (!row.hidden) count++;
    }
    const result = document.querySelector('#coverage-count');
    if (result) result.textContent = `${count} of 588 original questions`;
  };
  search?.addEventListener('input', apply); status?.addEventListener('change', apply);
</script>
<style>
  .coverage-table { overflow: auto; margin: 1rem 0; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .85rem; text-align: left; }
  th, td { padding: .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--bg-card); }
  .coverage-ledger { max-height: 42rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .coverage-ledger th { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1; }
  .coverage-ledger td:first-child { min-width: 15rem; max-width: 35rem; }
  details { margin-top: .4rem; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .75rem; }
  .coverage-filters { display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
  .coverage-filters label { display: block; flex: 1; font-size: .8rem; }
  input, select { display: block; width: 100%; margin: .4rem 0; background: var(--bg-input); color: var(--text-primary); font: inherit; padding: .7rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .coverage-plan li { margin: 1rem 0; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .coverage-filters { flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
